  "raw": " And if you agree with most of its big picture they will be quite very impressed and will probably spend your turn telling other people about it! If not – well ah well.\n\nBut as a sport this may take much more than that to disentangle; perhaps in the end we still won't know exactly what goes on under the covers in any given Test match or ODI or T20 contest: charlatans will remain that way, in spite of data gathering and the all-conquering pooling and stacking of data by game authorities, trainers etc.; and the more unforgiving nature of vicarious disappointment is often worse in sports which have been relentlessly commercialised and the actual play itself compromised for cash\n\nMany of us who slogged our guts out day after day to deflect palm shivers, batter batsmen and fielders today smiled as statesman Ian Chappell tried hard to disassociate the VAFA (Valuable Australian Fast-Bowling Allotment)",
  "serialized": "And if you agree with most of its big picture they will be quite very impressed and will probably spend your turn telling other people about it! If not – well ah well. But as a sport this may take much more than that to disentangle; perhaps in the end we still won't know exactly what goes on under the covers in any given Test match or ODI or T20 contest: charlatans will remain that way, in spite of data gathering and the all-conquering pooling and stacking of data by game authorities, trainers etc.; and the more unforgiving nature of vicarious disappointment is often worse in sports which have been relentlessly commercialised and the actual play itself compromised for cash Many of us who slogged our guts out day after day to deflect palm shivers, batter batsmen and fielders today smiled as statesman Ian Chappell tried hard to disassociate the VAFA (Valuable Australian Fast-Bowling Allotment)",
